---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'July 30, 2026';
---

<PageLayout
	title="Privacy — Epicenter"
	description="Where Epicenter stores your data, and when a service receives it."
	contained
>
	<div class="legal">
		<p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
		<h1 class="title-xl">Privacy</h1>
		<p class="stamp-line">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>

		<div class="body read">
			<p>
				The short version: your work starts on your device. A copy leaves it
				only when you choose a service that needs one.
			</p>

			<p>
				Epicenter is local-first software, and I build it in the open. Its tools
				keep working from data stored on your device. If you do not enable
				Epicenter's hosted sync, Epicenter does not receive a synchronized copy
				of that data.
			</p>

			<p>
				If you enable hosted sync, a server Epicenter runs stores a readable
				copy so your other devices can catch up. It is not end-to-end encrypted:
				operators of that server can read the synchronized data. If you run the
				sync server yourself, the readable server copy stays on infrastructure
				you control.
			</p>

			<p>
				Some tools can send data to a service you choose. For example,
				Whispering can send audio to a cloud transcription provider. That
				service receives only the data needed for the request and handles it
				under its own privacy terms. You can instead choose a local provider
				when one is available.
			</p>

			<p>
				This website records page views through PostHog so I can see which pages
				get visited. Interaction capture, session recording, user profiles, and
				persistent browser storage are disabled, and Do Not Track is respected.
				These analytics touch the public website, never data inside the tools.
			</p>

			<p>
				If you have questions, I would genuinely like to hear them:
				<a class="link" href="mailto:hello@epicenter.so">hello@epicenter.so</a>,
				or open an issue on
				<a class="link" href="https://github.com/EpicenterHQ/epicenter"
					>GitHub</a
				>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</PageLayout>

<style>
	.legal {
		max-width: 36rem;
		margin-inline: auto;
		padding-block: 3.25rem 0;
	}

	.legal .title-xl {
		margin-top: 0.85rem;
	}

	.stamp-line {
		margin-top: 0.9rem;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.04em;
		color: var(--ink-faint);
	}

	.body {
		margin-top: 2.25rem;
	}

	.body p + p {
		margin-top: 1.1rem;
	}
</style>
